%% STATUS: IMPLEMENTED. Speech uses a signed token, not a turn lookup. Normal inquiry (2026-11-05, branch platform-phases).
sequenceDiagram
  actor C as Caller
  participant V as Voice UI
  participant API as Calls API
  participant S as Safety engine
  participant O as Orchestrator
  participant AG as Agent
  participant L as LLM
  participant RV as Response validator
  participant TT as TTS
  participant DB as Postgres
  C->>V: Start Call
  V->>API: POST /api/calls
  API->>DB: Insert call, state GREETING
  API-->>V: callId, signed call token, notice and greeting
  V-->>C: Spoken notice and greeting
  C->>V: Speaks a question
  V->>API: POST /api/calls/id/turns with transcript
  API->>API: Verify token, validate, rate limit
  API->>DB: Insert caller turn
  API->>S: Check input
  S-->>API: LOW, general_product
  API->>O: Route using server-held state
  O->>AG: Selected agent with allowed capabilities
  AG->>L: Prompt and history window
  L-->>AG: Structured reply
  AG-->>O: Parsed contract
  O->>RV: Validate
  RV-->>O: Passed
  O->>DB: Insert validated agent turn
  O-->>API: turnId, text, agent
  API-->>V: turnId, text, agent
  V->>API: POST speech for turnId
  API->>DB: Fetch validated text
  API->>TT: Validated text
  TT-->>V: Audio stream
  V-->>C: Plays reply
